      "id": 202,
      "options": {
        "content": "**Cursors** are iterator-like objects used for traversing tries during state root calculation. Fast cursor operations are critical for performance.\n\n- **Trie Cursors**: Navigate account and storage trie branch nodes (seek, next, seek_exact)\n- **Hashed Cursors**: Access leaf data (accounts, storage values) by hash (seek, next, is_storage_empty)\n\nSlow cursor operations directly impact state root calculation time. Watch for patterns: many `seek` calls may indicate non-sequential access.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "8.0.0",
      "transparent": true,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "datasource": "prometheus",
      "description": "Frequency of cursor operations. High rates during state root calculation are normal. 'next' should dominate (sequential access is faster than random seeks).",
